From f55b9f6487117a9e7fd989f42d2d269b9c39aef5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: beardedeagle <randy@heroictek.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 19:47:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: Add Elixir extraction and resolution

Index Elixir (.ex, .exs) with the tree-sitter-elixir grammar from the
locked tree-sitter-wasms dependency (0.1.13), copied into
src/extraction/wasm like the other grammars. Extraction is adapted from
colbymchenry/codegraph#228 at 7314edc and extended:

- modules, nested modules, and protocols; functions and macros by name
  and arity, with guarded heads, default arguments forwarded as their
  own arities, and multi-clause functions merged into one source range;
- calls through lexical alias and explicit import scopes, including
  file-level and replacing re-imports; a do/end block counts as its
  implicit keyword argument; pipelines and ExUnit test bodies are call
  sites.

Resolution matches only the exact module/function/arity identities that
extraction supplies, keeps those candidates through all three resolver
normalization paths, resolves private functions and macros only from
their own module, and never guesses by bare name or suffix. Dynamic
module receivers and quoted macro data produce no call edges.

This is static analysis, not compiler evaluation: macro expansion,
protocol dispatch, anonymous-function dispatch, and dynamic modules are
out of scope, and operator definitions and ambiguous zero-argument calls
may be missed. Elixir runs on the WASM extraction path; the native
kernel is unchanged. EXTRACTION_VERSION moves to 28 so existing indexes
refresh.

Tests: Elixir extraction and graph suites, and resolution cases for the
Elixir matcher.
